In `_checkSolvencyAtTicks`, when `safeMode > 0`, overwrite utilizations for *every* element of `positionBalanceArray`, not just index 0. Example:
```solidity
if (safeMode > 0) {
  uint32 maxUtil = uint32(DECIMALS + (DECIMALS << 16));
  for (uint256 j = 0; j < positionBalanceArray.length; ++j) {
    positionBalanceArray[j] = PositionBalanceLibrary.storeBalanceData(
      positionBalanceArray[j].positionSize(),
      maxUtil,
      0
    );
  }
}
```
Also consider adding a regression test: safe mode solvency should be invariant to position ordering in the provided list.
